an-mcdonald","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Business - Consideration of Legislation - Speed things along","noes":12,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?gid=2019-12-05.79.5) to speed up consideration of two bills: * [Australian Crime Commission Amendment (Special Operations and Special Investigations) Bill 2019](https://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r6457); and * [Special Recreational Vessels Bill 2019](https://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r6459). In parliamentary jargon, they voted to suspend the usual [standing orders](https://peo.gov.au/understand-our-parliament/how-parliament-works/parliament-at-work/standing-orders/) - that is, the usual procedural rules - that would have delayed the bills passage through parliament. ### Motion text > *That the provisions of paragraphs (5) to (8) of standing order 111 not apply to the following bills, allowing them to be considered during this period of sittings:* > > *(1) Australian Crime Commission Amendment (Special Operations and Special Investigations) Bill 2019* > > *...* > > *(5) Special Recreational Vessels Bill 2019.*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-6158","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2019-12-05/7"}
